  "hindi": "सत्य को रचनेवाले देव के लिए, प्रेरक इन्द्र के लिए, जो अहि का हनन करनेवाला है, जल रुके नहीं। प्रतिदिन जलों का अक्तु चलता है; इनका पहला प्रवाह कितनी दूर तक है?",
  "english": "For the god who makes the order, for the impeller, for Indra the serpent-slayer, the waters did not come to rest. Day after day the aktu of the waters goes; how far does the first course of these extend?",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "'aktuḥ' is of uncertain sense (night, ray, ointment); left as aktu in the translation. 'kiyāti ā prathamaḥ sargaḥ āsām' is rendered 'how far (does) the first course of these (extend)'; the role of ā is uncertain. 'savitre' is taken as an epithet ('impeller') of Indra; it might be the god Savitṛ. 'ṛtam ... kṛṇvate' literally 'making order/right'.",
  "confidence": "low"
 },
