  "hindi": "जो यहाँ वृत्र के लिए सिन ले आता, उसे जाननेवाले की माता ने प्रकट कर दिया। मार्गों को काटती हुई गरजती धाराएँ प्रतिदिन उसके आनन्द के अनुसार लक्ष्य की ओर जाती हैं।",
  "english": "The mother of the knowing one declared him who would have brought sina here for Vṛtra. Cutting paths, the roaring ones go day by day to the goal, according to his pleasure.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "'sinam' is of uncertain sense (food, provision, bond) and is left as sina in the translation. 'viduṣaḥ' is taken as genitive with janitrī ('mother of the knowing one'); the knowing one is not named in the verse. 'pra ... uvāca' taken as 'declared'. 'dhunayaḥ' taken as 'roaring ones' (streams), with radantīḥ in agreement; 'asmai' is 'for him' without a stated referent.",
  "confidence": "low"
 },
