  "hindi": "हे बृहस्पति, तपते हुए पत्थर के समान, असुर के वृकद्वरस वीरों को बींध दो। जैसे तुमने पहले भी साहस से मारा था, वैसे ही, हे इन्द्र, हमारे शत्रु को मारो।",
  "english": "O Bṛhaspati, pierce with burning, as it were with a stone, the vṛkadvarasaḥ heroes of the asura. As you struck boldly before, so strike our enemy, O Indra.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "'tapuṣā aśneva' is rendered 'with burning, as it were with a stone'; tapuṣā is uncertain (burning, heat; possibly an adjective). 'vṛkadvarasaḥ' is left untranslated: the compound (wolf- + dvaras) is not understood. The second line addresses Indra while the first addresses Bṛhaspati, as printed. 'cit evā' read as cid evā; 'jaghantha' as 2 sg. pf. of han.",
  "confidence": "low"
